When the user wants the product built from the written specs, follow the implement-spec skill:

1. Read SKILL.md in this folder in full. It is an implement-only workflow.
2. Do not interview. Do not write a new product spec. Do not wait for approval.
3. Product specs in spec/01 through spec/17 are already approved. Implement them.
4. One MVP stage per request. Default to the first incomplete stage (usually Stage 1).
5. Read spec/01–04 for context, then only the stage files you are building.
6. Start writing code in the same turn. Keep progress in spec/impl/, not by editing spec/01–17.
7. Stack: FastAPI, Postgres + pgvector, S3, SQS, Bedrock via boto3, React talking only to the API.
8. Hackathon cuts: no login, no OCR, no dashboard. Keep company_id on tenant data.
9. Verify with pytest and ruff check . Do not commit unless the user asks.

Trigger this process when the user asks to: implement the specs, implement spec, start coding,
build the MVP, build stage 1–6, continue or resume implementation, code from the specs, or make
the app from the specs.
